Someone mentioned somewhere about wishing for a PYEC as a first wish.
Then I believe Mr. Dubois (sp?) said that the valkyrie in question
should have wished for a pair of GoP.
Well....
I would have done this:

Waited until my hp were about 50, where I could receive the blast of
power when you pick up or wish for a PYEC.
Recharge the wand with the PYEC (once the wand is out of charges).
Wish for a wand of polymorph.

A few hundred turns later with the gnomish mines, you have:
  shield of reflection
  helm of telepathy/esp/brilliance
  gauntlets of power
  boots of speed
  bag of holding

Plus, you can polymorph all those scrolls of teleport you keep finding,
and sometimes you end up with :

q - 12 scrolls of enchant armor

Not to mention a very low ac as a result.

So, yes, IMHO, the valkyrie did the correct thing in wishing for a 
PYEC.  Only her timing was bad.

Note: This only works if you are Neutral.

